One rendered type spells both an exported alias and its unexported target: the alias is
reachable but the target is not, and the walk must judge each spelling on its own name.
The visited set keys on type identity, under which an alias equals its target, so
checking the alias before the dedup is what keeps the exported spelling from swallowing
the unexported one. This ordering (alias first in the walk) is the one that would escape
under an identity-keyed-only walk.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrUnreachableType
-- example.com/lib/lib.go --
package lib

type hidden struct{ X int }
type Exported = hidden
type Thing struct{}

//plumb:build
func New(m map[Exported]hidden) *Thing { return &Thing{} }
